The Witcher 3 is out very soon and part  of the reason for the series success is  thanks to the engaging narrative take it  from Andrei slipped off skis novels now  that's not vyas example but here are 5  other games who've decided to take a  leaf out of someone's book that was  cheesy but I'm sticking with it backups  the line may not have had the best  shooting mechanics but it did have a  really cool story inspired by heart of  darkness Joseph Conrad's novella from  1899 the story of spec ops the line  follows Captain Martin Walker's journey  to do by now desolate and enveloped in  stand and his attempt to uncover what  happened to Colonel John Conrad it turns  the shooter genre on its head in a  really clever way and the story is just  littered with twists and exploration  into the human psyche a lot of these  concepts are taken from heart of  darkness which I've personally found to  be a bit of a slog but it must have been  good because it also inspired the film  Apocalypse Now as well as far cry 2  another novel with more adaptations than  you can shake a pocket watch at is Lewis  Carroll's Alice in Wonderland from 1865  a personally my favorite of those is  American McGee's Alice the events of  American McGee's Alice take place after  those written by Lewis Carroll although  in the video game [ __ ] seems to have hit  the fan in a big way Alice accidentally  burned a house down and her family along  with it was committed to a mental asylum  and fell into a delirium where her mind  now resides in a grim and twisted  version of Wonderland American McGee  expanded upon the darker themes present  in Carol's original story in a big way  and it works so well from the  reimagining of the now skeletal Cheshire  cat to the delightfully stubborn and  headstrong attitude of Alice in both  versions  despite her very different circumstances  dark post apocalyptic novels do seem  like they'd make pretty good videogames  and in the case of Metro 2033 the source  material was so good that they decided  to stick pretty damn close to it the  novel of the same name written by Dmitry  Glukhovsky takes place in  post-apocalyptic Moscow the story  follows Artyom Adair born into the world  of dank subway tunnels who goes on an  adventure traversing the hostile  irradiated world and it's threatening  inhabitants Metro 2033 was originally  released online where it became kind of  an interactive experiment budding  authors from all around the world would  write their own stories based in the  Metro universe featuring different  characters and genres all of which were  a hundred percent supported by the  author eventually for a games decided to  put their own spin on the universe by  turning Artyom story into a hardcore  first-person shooter helping the world  of Metro reach new heights of popularity  like Alice sometimes the game can serve  as a direct sequel to a book such was  the case with hideous sinners parasite  eve the book is all about evil  mitochondria taking over people and  animals until they become monsters  there's also a Czech called Eve made up  of said evil mitochondria who makes  people explode if they get too close to  and you have to kill her off before she  has a scary monster baby hell-bent on  human annihilation it's all very  Japanese the game by Final Fantasy dev  Squaresoft  took a few cues from Resident Evil and  introduced cop aya brea on a mission to  get rid of those very monsters from new  york city it also spawned two more  sequels of its own parasite eve - and  the third birthday  and finally we have Tom Clancy's Rainbow  six now the book and the game were  actually worked on at the same time and  they informed each other but the legacy  of the game still lives on to this day  the Rainbow six game spawned an entire  franchise made Tom Clancy a household  name in video games and basically wrote  the book on the tactical shooter and I  apologize my inability to avoid writing  cliches in any case Rainbow six made  gamers take their time to plan their  tactical approach to a mission before  actually going in and encouraged stealth  infiltrations in a way that was  basically unheard of in gaming so far  both the original game and the book  roughly followed the same plots where  the team must hunt down a terrorist unit  who want to release a mutated Ebola  virus at the Olympic Games  while our good guys end up on top either  way the video game was finished before  the book so the endgame plot does differ  let me know down in the comments which  game based on a novel is your favorite  and why also be sure to let me know if  there's any awesome games based on books  that I missed out on I'll catch you  again next week  you
 

